                <pb facs="0814" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg804"/>

                <head>(F.)—Mr. Walsh to Mr.
                        Magee.</head>
                <p>I do hereby certify that the thirty-one kegs of specie, marked B.M., containing
                    each $5,000, together $155,000, handed over to you by this institution for the
                    purpose of having the same delivered to H. Bell, consul general at Havana, and
                    to be transmitted thence to England to the consignment of the Union Bank of
                    London by the British mail steamer, is for the purpose of paying dues to British
                    subjects from the State of Alabama, and is the property and belongs to the
                    subjects of her Britannic Majesty.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES WALSH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
